From c9ad13b4da8021a464faf1be01e086e4ee0c8858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild Idler Patch <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 04:55:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Achievement expansion: per-chain, per-raid, vendor/guild
 completion, Grimsby, Harvest, Pets, Prestige (16 -> 65 total)

- 28 new per-quest-chain completion achievements (every chain except
  world_ender, already covered by WORLDS_END), auto-generated via a loop
  over QUEST_CHAINS rather than 28 hand-written checks. Names reuse each
  chain's own in-fiction title field directly. 5 marked hidden as
  genuine mystery/reveal or pre-capstone chains.
- 7 new per-raid clear achievements (every raid except requiem_last_god,
  covered by LAST_GOD_DEFEATED), same auto-loop treatment. what_got_out
  and silence_the_loom marked hidden (both built around a reveal).
- 5 vendor/guild completion achievements: Blacksmith/Alchemist/Enchanter
  maxed, all 8 Guild facilities maxed, and a grand COMPLETIONIST
  achievement requiring literally everything maxed at once.
- 4 Grimsby/Peddler achievements: first flip, jackpot hit, High Roller
  unlocked, jackpot while playing High Roller. Needed 3 new Statistics
  counters (peddlerFlips/peddlerJackpots/peddlerHighRollerJackpots),
  incremented in PeddlerManager.resolveFlip. SAVE_VERSION 35->36 with a
  migration backfilling all three for existing saves.
- 2 Harvest achievements (Warehouse maxed, all tools maxed) and 2 Pet
  achievements (first pet, full menagerie) directly answering this same
  review's own finding that those systems were under-covered.
- 1 Prestige achievement (5+ retirements), a third axis alongside the
  existing RETIREMENT_PARTY and ON_A_ROLL.

Found and fixed 8 real, pre-existing checkAll gaps while wiring this up:
pickPeddlerCard, unlockHighRoller, buyUpgrade, levelUpVendor,
upgradeFacility, upgradeHarvestTool, upgradeWarehouse, and hatchEgg in
engine.ts never called AchievementManager.checkAll, so nothing those
actions could satisfy would have unlocked at the actual moment it became
true. Also caught unlockHighRoller was missing notify() entirely. Merged
cleanly alongside the separately-landed notification/guidance patch,
which fixed the same class of gap for GuidanceManager in two of the same
methods (buyUpgrade, upgradeFacility) -- both checkAll calls now coexist
there.

Also logs the full Steam-launch completeness assessment as a tracked
backlog list (TESTING_TOOLS_ENABLED flag, missing single-instance lock,
asset licensing confirmation, Steamworks stub, art/icon population,
stale project-brief numbers, checkAll audit follow-up).

Verified at runtime: 65 total achievements, no duplicate ids; every
chain/raid achievement resolves and fires correctly and only for its own
completion; vendor/facility-maxed achievements fire independently and
COMPLETIONIST requires genuinely everything; Harvest/Pet/Prestige/
Peddler achievements fire from exactly the right state and not a lesser
version of it; the SAVE_VERSION migration backfills correctly while
preserving existing stats and composing correctly with the other team's
own new lastBannerShownId field. Full tsc --noEmit and vite build pass
clean.
